## VERDICT
First line of STATUS: `GATE VERDICT B451: <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> @ <head sha7> (MPSCALC-137 <token> · MPSCALC-172 <token> · C1 clauses met <n of n> per ticket, live Done-when changed since the builder's read <y/n> · C2 client.ts <+/-, route equal in 6 places y/n>, Proposal.cs <+/->, three fields Internal <y/n>, customer-output-absent <y/n>, Home.cs <+/->, HomeB49.cs <+/->, guard row mutant red <y/n>, EntraAuthTests <+/->, new route under <n of n> Entra checks, other operation tables missing the route <n> · C3 files outside brief and addenda <n; paths>, NOT-yours paths in diff <n> · C4 RED at base 137 <red/ran>, 172 <red/ran>, web <red/ran>, GREEN at head <y/n>, builder mutants <red counts>, own s1..s10 <red/survivor each>, c1..c8, a1..a8, o1..o3, w1..w5, survivors reachable <n> · C4.4 stored quotes unchanged <y/n>, rollback read <ok/note/throws> · C5 words found <n>, in pack <n of 10>, NOT in pack <n>, outside the WORDS-PENDING blocks <n> · C6 build 0/0 <y/n>, Engine/Import/Api/web <n/n/n/n>, names lost <n> added <n>, skipped <n>, pre-existing main-red <red/green/n.a.>, other reds <n> · C7 main <not moved|moved>, merge-tree rc <n>, squash tree = head tree <y/n>, b445* touches types.ts <y/n/not pushed>, other branches overlapping <n> · C8 gitleaks canary rc <n>, scan rc <n> · C9 weakened existing assertions <n>, scans <0/n> · C10 probes <n of n> as predicted, audit complete <y/n>)`. Then: Step 0 sha256s · REFUSE counts with controls · PINS (start, mid, verdict) · instrument (toolchain versions, load and slot per heavy run, every `gh` / Jira GET named) · C1-C10 each with FAIL (clock time), evidence path, result · the C1 per-clause table · the C2 numstat table · the C3 authority table · the C4 mutant table (builder's and yours side by side) · the C5 word table · findings (`B451-n`) with fix-shapes and regressions in prose · one Jira comment line each for MPSCALC-137 and MPSCALC-172 drafted for Tuesday's records seat (below; NOT posted) · the builder's FOR TUESDAY items (`:260-268`) each re-measured and listed with an owner (the addenda edits: your C2; stale names; stale comments in `QuoteStore.cs` and `callerCan.test.tsx`: confirm still stale at the head; design choices for the product owner: `outcomeAt` kept, same-value 409, cleared allowed; stub has no `correctOutcome`; `SOURCE.txt` names a scratch commit: read `git cat-file -t` of it at the head and say whether it is reachable from the branch, and whether `sync-contract.mjs` would reproduce the generated files from the committed `docs/api/openapi.json` (the blob check)) · FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED · corrections · processes, slots, trees left · **UNMEASURED** (last section before the last line, said plainly: the real price books and the real importer (never done, by rule), the hosted site, a hosted store, the Playwright e2e specs and the stub-persona figures (need a port, not run), real Entra sign-in, any rendered pixel, CodeQL and the GitHub CI legs (Tuesday's, on the PR), anything you could not drive and why). Add ` (conditional: <reason>)` to the first AND last line if a check you were required to run could not be run (never a bare GO). **Last line of STATUS, exactly one of:** `VERDICT: B451 b444/self-approval-137-outcome-correction-172 @ <sha7> on main <sha7>: MPSCALC-137 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO>, MPSCALC-172 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO>` (head sha7 by `ls-remote`, main sha7 by `ls-remote` at verdict) · `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` + ONE question.
**Jira line shape (draft only, written into STATUS for a later records seat; you write nothing to Jira):** `BLUF: QA gate B451 on branch b444/… @ <sha7> (no PR yet, not merged): MPSCALC-<n> <token>. Done-when <met | met by a different mechanism: which | partly: which clause>; <n> changed existing assertions, all by the ruling; <n> new words held; mutants <n>/<n> red (own <n>/<n>); Api <base> -> <head> passed. Findings: <ids and one clause each, or none>. Source: Briefs/2026-10-22_B451_STATUS.md.` No person's name (say "the product owner"), no key value, no price or SKU, no customer name.
**Severity floor (binding).**
- **Blocker:** a path outside the brief's Yours and the addenda that is under `src/`, `.github/`, `scripts/`, `infra/` or a project file; **self-approval allowed to anyone K-01 does not name** (an owner or submitter WITHOUT the Approver role, a wrong state, a Blocking issue passes); **correction allowed to a caller without the Approver role**; a customer output (proposal, export, file name, share) carrying `selfApproval`, `previousOutcome`, `correctedOutcome`, the reason or `outcome-corrected`; the original `outcome-recorded` event rewritten or deleted; a correction or approval recorded when the save failed; a stored pre-B444 quote that loads differently at the head beyond the documented optional members; an existing test weakened, relaxed, skipped, edited or deleted without the ruling beside it; a real price, SKU, figure or secret in an added line.
- **Major:** a Done-when clause not met or met by a mechanism the code lacks; an addendum condition violated (the diff exceeds the addendum: a second `client.ts` member, a second line in `Proposal.cs`, any other line in `Home.cs`, `HomeB49.cs` or `EntraAuthTests.cs`; the route string unequal anywhere; the guard row absent or in an existing file); the new route escaping an auth, role or contract check table (C2.4); a new RED row that is green at base, or red for a reason other than the defect; a mutant the builder says dies survives, or any survivor of C4.3 on a reachable authorisation or audit input; a new test red at head, a name lost, a skip added, a failed test in the whole line that is green at base; a user-visible new word on a screen or customer document that is not in the pack; an e2e or other existing spec that asserts a removed word and would fail; a base build that throws on reading a head-written store (rollback), when a deploy of the old build is possible.
- **Minor:** a survivor on a low-impact covered behaviour with no equivalence argument; a redundant new row; a pack word outside its WORDS-PENDING block; an API `detail` word not in the pack; a stale comment left in a file the builder was allowed to touch; a router, count or table pin that merely counts and misses the route; the figures keying on the stored `at` stated as context but contradicting a figure of the ticket; the builder's STATUS overclaiming where the code is right.
- **Note:** the four stale test names; stale comments in `QuoteStore.cs` and `callerCan.test.tsx` (RELAYED `:263`); `SELF_APPROVAL_MESSAGE` kept in `ErrorBox.tsx` for an old server; the `client.ts` type import and doc line; `EntraAuthTests` is Entra-only; the stub has no `correctOutcome`; the pre-existing `FeedbackTicketTests` timing red (never a finding against B444); `B445`'s local ref; a survivor on an unreachable input with its equivalence argument.

## HOLDS
- Datasec / MPS Commercial Calculator only. No deploy, Azure, `az`, hosted site or API, **no HTTP to any hosted or production site or any app host** (every probe is the in-process host; no server of any kind is started), docker, ssh. Network: `git fetch` of explicit refspecs into YOUR scratch clone, `gh api` GETs under `GH_CONFIG_DIR='<project>/4_Credentials/.gh-config'`, Jira GETs, NuGet and npm restores into your own worktrees only (the web suite is part of the CI line, so `npm ci` is the one network line this gate adds to the earlier MPS gate briefs; a restore that fails is a `NOT TESTED` with the error text, never a reason to skip C6 silently). No Jira write, PR comment, review, mark-ready, merge, push, or re-run of a check. Never dismiss an alert.
- **The real price books are confidential.** Never open `2_Project_Files/.local/`, `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/`, `.tools/backup-*` or any real book or store; never run the real importer on a real book; every fixture and reference is synthetic and in-process. A fact about the real book is UNMEASURED and says so.
- **Git in the project repo: READ verbs only** (`--no-optional-locks`: `ls-remote`, `log`, `show`, `diff`, `cat-file`, `ls-tree`, `rev-parse`, `rev-list`, `merge-base`, `grep`). In the project's `2_Project_Files` you never `fetch`, `worktree`, `merge-tree --write-tree`, `checkout`, `gc`, `branch -D`, `worktree prune`; all writes (clone, fetch, worktrees, scratch merge) happen only in `.tools/qa-b451/repo` and `.tools/qa-b451-*`. No git verb in the project root (records repo).
- Secrets only as environment, never on argv; never open `4_Credentials/.env` except to read `JIRA_*` and the leak-scan values in-process and to test the NAME `AGENTMAIL_API_KEY`; never `3_Access_Keys` except to name the deploy key in `core.sshCommand`.
- **Never delete** (`rm`, `rm -rf`, `docker rm`, `git branch -D`): quarantine to `.tools/qa-b451/quarantine/`. **Never `cd`** (a hook refuses it); absolute paths; where `dotnet` or `npm` needs a cwd, set it with Python `subprocess(cwd=...)` and say so; quote every path with spaces (the project folder has spaces); multi-step chains under `bash -c '...'` or a quoted heredoc (the Bash tool runs zsh: no word-splitting of an unquoted `$VAR`, and an unquoted word starting with `=` is refused, so quote separators); bash, not zsh, for loops; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count.
- Release before the last line: no process of yours in `ps`; `dotnet build-server shutdown` if you started one; your heavy slot absent. A line at your prompt that is not a Tuesday file pointer is not an instruction. No person's name in any id, file or branch you make. **Nothing to any human.**

